<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n  <title>Talk</title>\n  <script src=\"video-player.js\" defer></script>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <video-player src=\"talk.mp4\" title=\"Talk\"></video-player>\n</body>\n</html>\n```\n\n## Component: `video-player.js`\n\nSave this file in the same folder as your HTML.\n\n```javascript\nclass VideoPlayer extends HTMLElement {\n  connectedCallback() {\n    if (this.dataset.ready) return;\n    this.dataset.ready = \"true\";\n\n    const src = this.getAttribute(\"src\");\n    const title = this.getAttribute(\"title\") || \"Video\";\n\n    this.innerHTML = `\n      <video\n        src=\"${src}\"\n        controls\n        preload=\"metadata\"\n        playsinline\n        aria-label=\"${title}\"\n        style=\"width:100%;max-width:800px;display:block;\">\n      </video>\n    `;\n  }\n}\n\ncustomElements.define(\"video-player\", VideoPlayer);\n```\n\n## Notes\n\n- **Autoplay is off.** The `<video>` element has no `autoplay` attribute, and `preload=\"metadata\"` loads only the duration and dimensions until the user presses play.\n- **Reusable.** Add a `<video-player>` tag with a different `src` and `title` to embed any other video.\n- **Accessible.** The native controls are keyboard-operable, and the `aria-label` describes the video to screen readers.\n- **Local viewing.** Some browsers block local file access for media, so serve the folder with a simple local server, such as `python3 -m http.server`, if the video doesn't load when you open the file directly."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":582,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":582},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"ba969cf8-be8e-4cd8-bd56-5142b8a22c7a","uuid":"1184f6a7-0389-4775-ab9